Package: IterativeHardThresholding
Type: Package
Title: Iterative Hard Thresholding Extensions to Cyclops
Version: 2.0.0
Date: 2026-11-16
Authors@R: c(
    person("Marc A.", "Suchard", email = "msuchard@ucla.edu", role = c("aut","cre")),
    person("Patrick", "Ryan", role = "aut"),
    person("Observational Health Data Sciences and Informatics", role = "cph")
    )
Maintainer: Marc A. Suchard <msuchard@ucla.edu>
Description: Fits large-scale regression models with at most a prespecified number of
  non-zero regression coefficients (L0 regression with an optional ridge term), using Cyclops.
  The model is the one of Chu et al (2020) <doi:10.1093/gigascience/giaa044>. Each support is fitted
  exactly, as in Newton hard-thresholding pursuit (Zhou, Xiu and Qi 2021,
  <https://jmlr.org/papers/v22/19-026.html>), and the search combines gradient hard-thresholding steps
  with swaps of weak and strong covariates, as in Zhu et al (2020) <doi:10.1073/pnas.2014241117>.
  The algorithm of Chu et al (2020) is also available as is.
